{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-witt-vector-lift","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:witt-vector-lift","kind":"definition","title":"Witt vector lift","uses":["papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-commutative-formal-group","papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-skewed-poisson-structure","papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-non-commutative-formal-group"],"cites":["references/fred2005","references/hazewinkel1978"],"tags":["witt-vector","formal-group","lift"],"leanRef":"fred2005:Fred2005.WittVectorLift","text":"witt-vector-lift.md","leanSource":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/witt-vector-lift.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:witt-vector-lift\"></a><p>A <strong>Witt vector lift</strong> is the structure produced by applying the Witt\nvector functor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">W</code> to a\n<a href=\"#def:commutative-formal-group\">commutative formal group</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H / \\mathbb{F}_p</code>\nequipped with a\n<a href=\"#def:skewed-poisson-structure\">skewed-Poisson structure</a>.  The result\nis a formal group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{G} / \\mathbb{Z}_p</code> whose generic fibre is a\n<a href=\"#def:non-commutative-formal-group\">non-commutative formal group</a> over\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}_p</code>, and which reduces to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H</code> modulo <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>.</p>\n<p>Reference: <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"fred2005\">[fred2005]</span>, Section 5; <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"hazewinkel1978\">[hazewinkel1978]</span>, Chapter V.</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/witt-vector-lift.md","heading":"Definition","number":"1.6.1"}
